# MemoryBox — File & View splitting

## Hard limits

- Prefer files **under 250 lines**. Soft warn at 300. Split before 400.
- `PersistenceController.swift` is legacy-fat — **do not add** new feature APIs there; put in `Services/*`.
- Do not dump multiple unrelated screens into `Editors.swift` / `HomeComponents.swift` for new work.

## Naming

| Kind | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Screen | `FooView.swift` |
| Section/subview | `FooHeaderView.swift`, `FooEmptyView.swift` |
| ViewModel | `FooViewModel.swift` |
| Service | `FooService.swift` |
| Coordinator | `FooCoordinatorView.swift` |

## Onboarding / Share

Follow `docs/onboarding-couple-share-flow.md`. New files go under:

- `Views/Onboarding/`
- `ViewModels/Onboarding/`

## Don't

- Don't create “Utils.swift” god files.
- Don't put ViewModels inside View files.
- Don't keep dead code “for later”.
